      "source": "docs/blueprint.md (Flow, F3); docs/conventions.md \u00a71.4 M1",
      "whatItForbidsHere": "`dab/mappings/customer-mapping.yaml` may read only `das__staged.customers` \u2014 never `das__raw.customers`, never a subquery, and never a join of orders to customers. The relationship is declared, not hand-joined: the ORDER\u2192CUSTOMER edge is expressed as a `relationships:` entry in the order mapping (`id`, `source_table`, `target_transformation_expression`), which is the shape daana documents (blog `doc-ch1.txt` lines 296-302). Writing the customer country onto ORDER by any expression that reads the customers table is forbidden twice over \u2014 by M1 and by M5."
