    {
      "rule": "M3 \u2014 `ingestion_strategy: FULL_LOG`; M4 \u2014 `entity_effective_timestamp_expression: extracted_at`",
      "source": "docs/conventions.md \u00a71.4 M3, M4; ADR 0004; spike 2 findings 7, 8, 9",
      "whatItForbidsHere": "The customers mapping may not use `FULL`. Observed in spike 2: `FULL` against a multi-row-per-key staged view inserts one duplicate `_desc` row per execute (22\u219223\u219224\u219225 across three runs) and every presentation view hides it. `das__staged.customers` is a change log by construction, so it is exactly the multi-row case. M4 forbids dating a CUSTOMER version by anything but `extracted_at` \u2014 and Northwind's Customer entity has no date property at all, so there is nothing else to be tempted by."
