      "source": "docs/conventions.md \u00a71.4",
      "whatItForbidsHere": "`customer-mapping.yaml` gets one primary key (`customer_id`), never two \u2014 two entries are two *alternate identifiers* to the engine and cannot be undone once loaded. M5 forbids deriving the customer's country inside the ORDER mapping by any expression that reaches the customers table. M7 means CUSTOMER must carry at least one attribute, so the entity cannot be added as identity-only in this slice."
