      "rule": "\u00a71.2 \u2014 a relationship name is a verb phrase, so `<SOURCE>_<NAME>_<TARGET>` reads as a sentence",
      "source": "docs/conventions.md \u00a71.2, whose own worked example is `ORDER_IS_PLACED_BY_CUSTOMER`",
      "whatItForbidsHere": "Forbids `ORDER_CUSTOMER`, `HAS_CUSTOMER`, `CUSTOMER_PLACES_ORDER` (wrong direction \u2014 the source entity must be ORDER, because the many-to-one edge runs order\u2192customer and that direction is what the generator walks). In `dab/model.yaml` the relationship block carries `name: IS_PLACED_BY`, `source_entity_id: ORDER`, `target_entity_id: CUSTOMER` (blog `doc-ch1.txt` line 174-178)."
